content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-105 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22000, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft seal leakage: the manual's troubleshooting table points to worn or cracked seal faces, a seal run dry or shaft misalignment. The action is to replace the mechanical seal (5.2) and check alignment (5.4). No leak-rate limit is documented, so seal replacement should be planned.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.9 mm/s against Figure 3 (mm/s RMS on bearing housings). The reading falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s, 'Long-term operation'). It is above the Zone A limit of 2.8 mm/s and below the Zone C boundary of 4.5 mm/s ('Restricted – plan maintenance') and the Zone D boundary of 7.1 mm/s ('stop the pump'). Vibration alone does not require a stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature 71 C against the specification limits (housing surface): normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C. The reading is 1 C above the normal limit and 9 C below alarm. It is elevated but does not require a stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Early failure of component seal HF3-450 is the most likely seal cause if that seal is fitted. AquaDyne field returns show early HF3-450 failure on pumps built from serial HF3-22000 onwards, caused by a revised sleeve tolerance. This pump is serial HF3-22000.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is the common cause listed for all three symptoms: seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces, or the seal having run dry. The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge and the seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing or bearing wear may explain the slightly elevated drive-end housing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation, are other listed causes of vibration. They are less likely here because the reading is still in Zone B.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Rig lifting equipment and remove the back pull-out assembly. It weighs 68 kg. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller. Inspect the impeller for damage, since impeller damage or imbalance is a listed vibration cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and shaft sleeve. Record the part number of the removed seal (HF3-450 or HF3-450B). Inspect the sleeve for scoring and replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new cartridge seal HF3-450B. Do NOT fit HF3-450 on this serial. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120. It must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten to the following torques on lightly oiled threads: impeller nut M24 160 Nm; seal gland nuts 30 Nm per SB-2026-014 (not the 25 Nm in Table 5); casing bolts M16 210 Nm; bearing housing bolts M12 85 Nm if disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, inspect both bearings and check the grease quantity. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair (HF3-512 drive-end 6312-C3 and HF3-510 non-drive-end 6310-C3).",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the shaft after reassembly. Alignment is called for in the seal-leak, vibration and temperature actions, and after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is working and the casing is primed and vented before start-up. Never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Confirm bearing housing temperature is back within normal (70 C or below).",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve – fit only if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 – contingency, fit as a pair with HF3-510 only if bearings show wear, noise or high temperature",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 – contingency, fit as a pair with HF3-512 only if bearings show wear",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate the pump (400 V, 55 kW motor) and drain it before starting work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not run the pump dry. The seal flush (Plan 11) must be established before start-up.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Until the repair is done, monitor drive-end housing temperature against the alarm (80 C) and trip (90 C) limits. Monitor vibration against the Zone C (4.5 mm/s) and Zone D (7.1 mm/s, stop the pump) boundaries.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency – bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians, only if bearings are found worn.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: the manual parts list (Revision D) gives HF3-450 component seal. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with cartridge seal HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above. This pump is serial HF3-22000, which falls within 'HF3-22000 and above', so the bulletin applies: use HF3-450B.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm. SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because this serial is covered by the bulletin and HF3-450B is being fitted, use 30 Nm. Table 5 still applies to all other fasteners.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve: manual 5.2 says only to inspect the sleeve for scoring. The bulletin adds a replacement criterion of scoring deeper than 0.1 mm and states no sleeve measurement is needed for the pre-set HF3-450B. Apply the bulletin criterion for this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which seal is currently fitted (HF3-450 or HF3-450B)? This decides whether the bulletin's early-failure cause applies.",
    "How severe is the leak (leak rate, trend)? No leakage limit is documented, so the urgency of a stop cannot be set from the evidence.",
    "Is the 3.9 mm/s reading an RMS velocity on a bearing housing, and is it the highest of both housings as Figure 3 requires?",
    "What is the non-drive-end housing temperature, and is the drive-end temperature trending?",
    "The evidence gives no grease type, grease quantity or regreasing interval for checking over-greasing.",
    "The evidence gives no torque for the motor or baseplate hold-down bolts used during alignment.",
    "Has the Plan 11 seal flush line been checked for blockage? It is a possible cause of the seal running dry."
  ]
}
